  "text": {
    "intro": "The Hollow Creek county fair runs its pie judging with more ceremony than the state legislature.\nFive bakers are involved. Determine each baker's placing, filling, county and crust.\n- **Baker**: Odette, Bramwell, Marigold, Winnie and Thaddeus.\n- **Placing** (listed from better to worse): first, second, third, fourth and fifth.\n- **Filling**: pecan, green tomato, rhubarb, mincemeat and sour cherry.\n- **Home county**: Quarry Hill, Little Pell, Fenwick, Dunmore and Hobbs Bend.\n- **Crust**: a cut-out star top, a fork-crimped edge, a fluted rim, a crumb topping and a lattice top.\nEvery baker has a different placing, filling, county and crust, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The baker who uses a fork-crimped edge is worse than third in placing order.",
      "Odette and the baker who bakes pecan are exactly four places apart in placing order.",
      "The baker who uses a cut-out star top does not bake green tomato. Thaddeus is exactly one place better than the baker who uses a cut-out star top, with no placing in between.",
      "The baker who comes from Fenwick is exactly one place better than the baker who bakes sour cherry, with no placing in between.",
      "The baker who comes from Quarry Hill falls somewhere between Winnie and the baker who uses a lattice top in placing order.",
      "Bramwell and the baker who uses a crumb topping are exactly three places apart in placing order.",
      "Winnie and the baker who bakes rhubarb are exactly one place apart in placing order, in one direction or the other.",
      "Thaddeus is better than the baker who uses a lattice top in placing order.",
      "At least one of the following holds, and possibly more than one: (a) Marigold comes from Quarry Hill. (b) The baker who comes from Hobbs Bend and the baker who bakes sour cherry both sit at odd-numbered places or both at even-numbered places.",
      "The baker who bakes sour cherry is exactly one place better than the baker who comes from Dunmore, with no placing in between.",
      "Thaddeus and the baker who bakes mincemeat are exactly four places apart in placing order.",
      "Bramwell is exactly one place better than the baker who comes from Dunmore, with no placing in between."
    ]
  }
